-----------------------------------------------------------------
Next N is a substantially re-engineered derivative work originally based on
v2rayN (Copyright (C) 2019-Present 2dust, licensed under GNU GPL v3.0).

Summary of major modifications made in 2026 by EbramJames:
- Unified cross-platform desktop architecture onto Avalonia 12 + .NET 10
  (retired legacy Windows-only WPF duplicate codebase).
- Completely redesigned modern sidebar navigation shell, theme tokens,
  brand identity, icons, and unified status/control dock.
- Replaced external GlobalHotKeys git submodule with a self-contained
  Win32 message-thread hotkey engine.
- Hardened SQLite query layer with parameterized queries, fixed dynamic
  Avalonia style accumulation leaks, fixed single-instance mutex lifetime
  on Unix platforms, and fixed non-Windows core chmod handling.
- Added native NSIS Windows Setup Installer with bundled Xray-core,
  sing-box, and GeoIP/GeoSite rule-sets, plus unified macOS DMG and Linux
  DEB / RPM / AppImage packaging pipelines.
- Removed bundled third-party promotional links and replaced them with a
  native About dialog and transparent GitHub release workflow.
